<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ebiri Moro</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ebiri Moro was a king of Aowin, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> state in the forest of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>. In the early 18th century, during a succession crisis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Asante</a>, his forces raided the Asante capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a>. The Ashanti Empire retaliated, defeating Aowin and overrunning the kingdom, and Ebiri Moro withdrew westward.</p></div>
